    >>> theta = jnp.linspace(-jnp.pi, jnp.pi, 9)
    >>> with jnp.printoptions(precision=2, suppress=True):
    ...   print(theta)
    [-3.14 -2.36 -1.57 -0.79  0.    0.79  1.57  2.36  3.14]

    These angles can equivalently be represented by ``(x, y)`` coordinates
    on a unit circle:

